turns.text:
I can’t complete this analysis with the available HPA tools.

The requested calculation requires the HPA **immune-cell sample RNA dataset**, including:

- donor/sample identifiers;
- NK-cell and memory CD8 T-cell sample assignments;
- per-sample nTPM values;
- the separate aggregate immune-cell file;
- the HPA master-table Ensembl-gene universe;
- the complete set of CD-marker genes.

The available tools provide gene-level or aggregate blood-expression lookups, but do not expose the donor-level immune-cell sample matrix or the required aggregate-file fields. Consequently, I cannot reliably calculate:

- matched-donor counts;
- per-donor median nTPM values;
- donor log2 changes and their summaries;
- retained-gene counts;
- paired-versus-aggregate Spearman correlation;
- opposite-sign gene counts;
- the fifteen disagreement-ranked genes;
- the requested heatmap, scatter plot, or bar chart.

Producing those values from the available endpoints would require estimating or substituting data, which would violate the requirement to base every number and gene list on HPA tool results.

